# Where the Black Ops 7 multiplayer weapon catalog comes from

Everything here was read on **2026-09-23**. `catalog.json` in this folder is the
list of every weapon a player can put in a Black Ops 7 **multiplayer** loadout;
this file says where every fact and every picture in it came from.

**Pictures: publisher artwork only (decision D116).** Every picture in
`weapons/` is Activision's own image, from callofduty.com or its image server
imgs.callofduty.com, converted to PNG, cropped to the weapon and scaled to at
most 480 x 300 pixels. 63 of them are byte-for-byte copies of the Black Ops 7
pictures in `../cod-warzone/weapons/` (the same weapons; each catalog folder is
self-contained, so they are copied, not shared), and their rows below are the
Warzone catalog's rows unchanged. One, the Roc 20mm, is new here. None came from
a fan wiki, Fandom, a loadout site or an image search. They are Activision's
copyright, used in the app to identify the weapon, the same risk the owner
accepted for the game pictures in D116. Delete a `.png` and set that weapon's
`image` to `null` and the app shows the class symbol instead; nothing else
changes.

## What is in Black Ops 7 multiplayer today

- **Current season: Season 06, "The Haunting"**, live since September 17, 2026
  ([Season 06 blog](https://www.callofduty.com/blog/2026/09/call-of-duty-black-ops-7-warzone-season-6-the-haunting-announcement),
  [Black Ops 7 Season 06 patch notes](https://www.callofduty.com/patchnotes/2026/09/call-of-duty-black-ops-7-season-06-patch-notes)).
  The notes call it "the final Season of Black Ops 7 Ranked Play".
- **Launch (November 14, 2025): 30 weapons**, 23 primary, 5 secondary, 2 melee
  ([launch weapons blog](https://www.callofduty.com/blog/2025/11/call-of-duty-black-ops-7-ready-for-launch-weapons-equipment)).
- **Every season since added weapons** (Black Ops 7's own patch notes and season
  blogs, table below): Season 01 seven (Kogot-7, Maddox RFB, Sokol 545, NX
  Ravager, Ballistic Knife, then Sturmwolf 45 and Hawker HX at Season 01
  Reloaded); Season 02 seven (REV-46, EGRT-17, H311-SAW, GDL Havoc, SG-12, then
  Voyak KT-3 and Swordfish A1 at Reloaded); Season 03 six (MK35 ISR, VST,
  Strider 300, 1911, then Siren and Katana); Season 04 six (KRS-7.62, CBRS-3,
  Grimhawk, VX Compact, then AN-94 and Executioner's Duet); Season 05 four
  (FG42, Gremlin, Mammoth, then Mace); Season 06 four (VMP, TR51 Para,
  Arcblade, Roc 20mm).

Counts: **64 weapons in 10 classes**: Assault Rifles 14, SMGs 13, Shotguns 4,
LMGs 4, Marksman Rifles 5, Sniper Rifles 5, Pistols 4, Launchers 2, Special 5,
Melee 8. All 64 have a picture.

## Black Ops 7 multiplayer against Warzone

Checked, not assumed:

- **Every Black Ops 7 weapon in Warzone is in multiplayer, and the reverse.**
  The 64 here are exactly the 64 Black Ops 7 weapons of `../cod-warzone/`. Each
  one is named, with its class, on a Black Ops 7 multiplayer page (the launch
  blog, a season blog, or the Black Ops 7 patch notes' "New Weapons" section),
  and the Warzone catalog finds each one on a Warzone page. No season added a
  weapon to only one of the two.
- **What Warzone has and multiplayer does not: the 206 Legacy weapons** (Black
  Ops 6, Modern Warfare III, Modern Warfare II). The Season 01 blog's Warzone
  section says they are "accessible in Call of Duty: Warzone (only)".
- **Not in this list, on purpose:**
  - Scorestreak weapons (Death Machine, War Machine, Grim Reaper, Archangel
    Launcher, Combat Bow and the others the Season 01 Reloaded notes add under
    "Returning Black Ops 6 Loadout Content"): they come from a Scorestreak, not
    from a loadout.
  - Zombies-only weapons: the Wonder Weapons, and the "Ultra-Rarity Legacy
    Weapons" that appear only in Zombies Mystery Boxes (the PPSh-41 from Season
    04 Reloaded, the TR2 and the Olympia from Season 05 Reloaded).
  - Weapon Blueprints and Mastercraft variants, even when an event names them
    like a weapon: Season 06's "DOOM Shotgun" and "Crucible Blade" are the
    "Tear" M10 Breacher and "Crucible" Katana Blueprints (Season 06 blog).
  - Equipment (the Combat Axe is a Lethal).

## How the list is organised, and what is not confirmed

- **Classes, in the game's order.** Activision's own [Black Ops 7 weapons
  guide](https://www.callofduty.com/guides/blackops7/weapons) filters by
  Assault Rifle, SMG, Shotgun, LMG, Marksman Rifle, Sniper Rifle, Pistol,
  Launcher, Special, Melee, the order the launch blog lists Primary, Secondary
  and Melee weapons in. The group ids and names are the Warzone catalog's (the
  plural the launch blog uses; "Special" as the guide and the patch-note class
  brackets write it), so a weapon has the same id in both catalogs.
- **Order inside a class**: the launch weapons first, the free one then by the
  player level that unlocks it (the launch blog's "Player Levels: Weapon Unlock
  Criteria"), then each later weapon in the order its season added it. **The
  order on the in-game screen itself was not confirmed** from an official page.
- **Ids** are the Warzone catalog's ids for the same weapons. They are permanent
  in each catalog on its own; sharing them only means a weapon trained in one
  game reads the same in the other.

## Names

Names are spelt as the Warzone catalog spells them, which is Activision's
spelling in running text (the launch blog first, then the season blogs and
patch-note text); every one was checked against the Black Ops 7 pages below.
The game draws weapon names in capitals, so capitalisation never changes what
the owner sees on screen. The Warzone catalog's `SOURCES.md` lists Activision's
own slips (A.R.C M1, Coda 9 / CODA 9, Flatline Mk.II / MK.II, Peacekeeper MK1 /
Mk1, M15 Mod 0 / MOD 0) and what was used instead; the same choices hold here.
The Season 01 blog also writes "Sturmwulf 45" twice and "Hawker HK" once, under
their camo pictures; its own headings and every other page say Sturmwolf 45 and
Hawker HX.

## Uncertain

- `pistols.coda_9` (Coda 9): Capitalisation only: Activision writes 'Coda 9' (launch blog, patch-note text) and 'CODA 9' (weapons guide, Season 01 notes) about equally; the game sets names in capitals, so both read the same on screen.
- `special.nx_ravager` (NX Ravager): Class: Activision's Season 01 blog calls it a Special Weapon (class line 'Special, Event Reward') and the Season 01 patch notes tune it under Special Weapons, but the Black Ops 7 weapons guide index labels it Sniper Rifle (its own picture there is named SPC). Filed under Special until the owner's screen says otherwise.
- `melee.flatline_mk_ii` (Flatline Mk.II): Capitalisation only: the launch blog writes 'Flatline Mk.II', several patch notes 'Flatline MK.II'; the game sets names in capitals.

## Community sites

None was needed: every weapon, class and spelling here is on an Activision
page. The Warzone catalog's `SOURCES.md` lists the community sites that were
read to cross-check the Black Ops 7 list (wzstats.gg matched it).

